BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
45 780 Td
(   = -sin^\(n-1\) x * cos x + \(n - 1\) * int sin^\(n-2\) x dx - \(n - 1\) * int sin^n x dx) Tj
T*
(   = -sin^\(n-1\) x * cos x + \(n - 1\) * I_{n-2} - \(n - 1\) * I_n.) Tj
T*
(   - Bring \(n - 1\)*I_n to the left-hand side:) Tj
T*
(   I_n + \(n - 1\)*I_n = -sin^\(n-1\) x * cos x + \(n - 1\) * I_{n-2}) Tj
T*
(   n * I_n = -sin^\(n-1\) x * cos x + \(n - 1\) * I_{n-2}) Tj
T*
(   I_n = - [ sin^\(n-1\) x * cos x ] / n + [ \(n - 1\) / n ] * I_{n-2}. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Deduction of Wallis' Formula over [0, pi/2]:) Tj
T*
(   - Let J_n = int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^n x dx.) Tj
T*
(   - The boundary term [ -sin^\(n-1\) x * cos x / n ]_0^\(pi/2\) vanishes at both limits:) Tj
T*
(   At pi/2: cos\(pi/2\) = 0. At 0: sin\(0\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore: J_n = [ \(n - 1\) / n ] * J_{n-2}.) Tj
T*
(   - Case 1: n is an odd positive integer \(n = 2k + 1\):) Tj
T*
(   J_n = [ \(n-1\)/n ] * [ \(n-3\)/\(n-2\) ] * ... * \(2/3\) * J_1.) Tj
T*
(   J_1 = int_0^\(pi/2\) sin x dx = [-cos x]_0^\(pi/2\) = 0 - \(-1\) = 1.) Tj
T*
(   Wallis formula \(odd n\): J_n = [ \(n-1\)\(n-3\)...\(2\) ] / [ n\(n-2\)...\(3\) ] * 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Case 2: n is an even positive integer \(n = 2k\):) Tj
T*
(   J_n = [ \(n-1\)/n ] * [ \(n-3\)/\(n-2\) ] * ... * \(1/2\) * J_0.) Tj
T*
(   J_0 = int_0^\(pi/2\) 1 dx = pi / 2.) Tj
T*
(   Wallis formula \(even n\): J_n = [ \(n-1\)\(n-3\)...\(1\) ] / [ n\(n-2\)...\(2\) ] * \(pi / 2\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
