(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the reduction formula for I_n = int cos^n x dx. Using Wallis' formula, evaluate: \(i\) int_0^\(pi/2\) cos^7 x dx, and \(ii\) int_0^\(pi/2\) cos^8 x dx.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Reduction Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - Let I_n = int cos^n x dx = int cos^\(n-1\) x * cos x dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrate by parts with u = cos^\(n-1\) x, dv = cos x dx:) Tj
T*
(   du = -\(n - 1\) * cos^\(n-2\) x * sin x dx, v = sin x.) Tj
T*
(   - I_n = cos^\(n-1\) x * sin x - int sin x * [ -\(n - 1\) * cos^\(n-2\) x * sin x ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = cos^\(n-1\) x * sin x + \(n - 1\) * int cos^\(n-2\) x * sin^2 x dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute sin^2 x = 1 - cos^2 x:) Tj
T*
(   I_n = cos^\(n-1\) x * sin x + \(n - 1\) * int cos^\(n-2\) x * \(1 - cos^2 x\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = cos^\(n-1\) x * sin x + \(n - 1\) * I_{n-2} - \(n - 1\) * I_n) Tj
T*
(   => n * I_n = cos^\(n-1\) x * sin x + \(n - 1\) * I_{n-2}) Tj
T*
(   => I_n = [ cos^\(n-1\) x * sin x ] / n + [ \(n - 1\) / n ] * I_{n-2}. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Definite Integral over [0, pi/2]:) Tj
T*
(   - Boundary term vanishes: J_n = [ \(n - 1\) / n ] * J_{n-2}.) Tj
T*
(   - By substitution x = pi/2 - t, int_0^\(pi/2\) cos^n x dx = int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^n t dt.) Tj
T*
(   3. Numerical Evaluations:) Tj
T*
(   - Part \(i\): Evaluate J_7 = int_0^\(pi/2\) cos^7 x dx \(n = 7, odd\):) Tj
T*
(   J_7 = \(6 / 7\) * \(4 / 5\) * \(2 / 3\) * 1) Tj
T*
(   = \(6 * 4 * 2\) / \(7 * 5 * 3\) = 48 / 105 = 16 / 35.) Tj
T*
(   - Part \(ii\): Evaluate J_8 = int_0^\(pi/2\) cos^8 x dx \(n = 8, even\):) Tj
T*
(   J_8 = \(7 / 8\) * \(5 / 6\) * \(3 / 4\) * \(1 / 2\) * \(pi / 2\)) Tj
T*
(   = \(7 * 5 * 3 * 1\) / \(8 * 6 * 4 * 2\) * \(pi / 2\)) Tj
T*
(   = 105 / 384 * \(pi / 2\) = 35 / 128 * \(pi / 2\) = 35*pi / 256.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   \(i\) int_0^\(pi/2\) cos^7 x dx = 16 / 35.) Tj
T*
(   \(ii\) int_0^\(pi/2\) cos^8 x dx = 35*pi / 256.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
