(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the reduction formula for I_{m,n} = int sin^m x * cos^n x dx. Hence, evaluate the definite integral: int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^6 x * cos^4 x dx.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Reduction Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - Let I_{m,n} = int sin^m x * cos^n x dx = int [ sin^m x * cos^\(n-1\) x ] * cos x dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrate by parts: let u = sin^m x * cos^\(n-1\) x and dv = cos x dx \(v = sin x\).) Tj
T*
(   du = [ m * sin^\(m-1\) x * cos x * cos^\(n-1\) x - \(n - 1\) * sin^m x * cos^\(n-2\) x * sin x ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = [ m * sin^\(m-1\) x * cos^n x - \(n - 1\) * sin^\(m+1\) x * cos^\(n-2\) x ] dx.) Tj
T*
(   - I_{m,n} = sin^m x * cos^\(n-1\) x * sin x - int sin x * du) Tj
T*
(   = sin^\(m+1\) x * cos^\(n-1\) x - m * int sin^m x * cos^n x dx + \(n - 1\) * int sin^\(m+2\) x *) Tj
T*
(   cos^\(n-2\) x dx.) Tj
T*
(   - In the last integral, write sin^\(m+2\) x = sin^m x * \(1 - cos^2 x\):) Tj
T*
(   int sin^\(m+2\) x * cos^\(n-2\) x dx = int sin^m x * cos^\(n-2\) x dx - int sin^m x * cos^n x dx) Tj
T*
(   = I_{m, n-2} - I_{m, n}.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute:) Tj
T*
(   I_{m,n} = sin^\(m+1\) x * cos^\(n-1\) x - m * I_{m,n} + \(n - 1\) * I_{m, n-2} - \(n - 1\) * I_{m,n}) Tj
T*
(   I_{m,n} * [ 1 + m + n - 1 ] = sin^\(m+1\) x * cos^\(n-1\) x + \(n - 1\) * I_{m, n-2}) Tj
T*
(   \(m + n\) * I_{m,n} = sin^\(m+1\) x * cos^\(n-1\) x + \(n - 1\) * I_{m, n-2}) Tj
T*
(   I_{m,n} = [ sin^\(m+1\) x * cos^\(n-1\) x ] / \(m + n\) + [ \(n - 1\) / \(m + n\) ] * I_{m, n-2}.) Tj
T*
(   \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Evaluation of int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^6 x * cos^4 x dx:) Tj
T*
(   - Over [0, pi/2], the boundary term vanishes since sin\(0\) = 0 and cos\(pi/2\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Wallis' formula for product:) Tj
T*
(   J_{m,n} = [ \(m-1\)\(m-3\)... * \(n-1\)\(n-3\)... ] / [ \(m+n\)\(m+n-2\)... ] * K,) Tj
T*
(   where K = pi / 2 if both m and n are even, and K = 1 otherwise.) Tj
T*
(   - Here m = 6 \(even\), n = 4 \(even\), so K = pi / 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Numerator:) Tj
T*
(   \(m - 1\)\(m - 3\)\(m - 5\) = \(5\)\(3\)\(1\) = 15.) Tj
T*
(   \(n - 1\)\(n - 3\) = \(3\)\(1\) = 3.) Tj
T*
(   Numerator product = 15 * 3 = 45.) Tj
T*
(   - Denominator:) Tj
T*
(   \(m + n\)\(m + n - 2\)... = \(10\)\(8\)\(6\)\(4\)\(2\) = 3840.) Tj
T*
(   - Result:) Tj
T*
(   J_{6,4} = [ 45 / 3840 ] * \(pi / 2\) = [ 3 / 256 ] * \(pi / 2\) = 3*pi / 512.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^6 x * cos^4 x dx = 3*pi / 512.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
