(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the reduction formulas for: \(i\) I_n = int tan^n x dx, and \(ii\) I_n = int sec^n x dx. Using these, evaluate int_0^\(pi/4\) tan^5 x dx and int sec^3 x dx.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Part \(i\): Reduction Formula for I_n = int tan^n x dx:) Tj
T*
(   - Write tan^n x = tan^\(n-2\) x * tan^2 x = tan^\(n-2\) x * \(sec^2 x - 1\):) Tj
T*
(   I_n = int tan^\(n-2\) x * sec^2 x dx - int tan^\(n-2\) x dx.) Tj
T*
(   - In the first integral, let u = tan x, du = sec^2 x dx:) Tj
T*
(   int u^\(n-2\) du = u^\(n-1\) / \(n - 1\) = tan^\(n-1\) x / \(n - 1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   I_n = [ tan^\(n-1\) x ] / \(n - 1\) - I_{n-2}. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluate J_5 = int_0^\(pi/4\) tan^5 x dx:) Tj
T*
(   J_5 = [ tan^4 x / 4 ]_0^\(pi/4\) - J_3 = [ 1^4 / 4 - 0 ] - J_3 = 1/4 - J_3.) Tj
T*
(   J_3 = [ tan^2 x / 2 ]_0^\(pi/4\) - J_1 = [ 1/2 ] - J_1.) Tj
T*
(   J_1 = int_0^\(pi/4\) tan x dx = [ ln\(sec x\) ]_0^\(pi/4\) = ln\(sqrt\(2\)\) - ln\(1\) = \(1/2\)*ln 2.) Tj
T*
(   J_3 = 1/2 - \(1/2\)*ln 2.) Tj
T*
(   J_5 = 1/4 - [ 1/2 - \(1/2\)*ln 2 ] = 1/4 - 1/2 + \(1/2\)*ln 2 = \(1/2\)*ln 2 - 1/4.) Tj
T*
ET

