(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the reduction formula for I_n = int x^n * e^\(a*x\) dx. Using this formula, evaluate the definite integral: int_0^1 x^4 * e^\(2x\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Reduction Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - Let I_n = int x^n * e^\(a*x\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrate by parts: let u = x^n and dv = e^\(a*x\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   du = n * x^\(n-1\) dx, v = \(1 / a\) * e^\(a*x\).) Tj
T*
(   - I_n = u * v - int v du) Tj
T*
(   = \(1 / a\) * x^n * e^\(a*x\) - int \(1 / a\) * e^\(a*x\) * n * x^\(n-1\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = \(1 / a\) * x^n * e^\(a*x\) - \(n / a\) * int x^\(n-1\) * e^\(a*x\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = \(1 / a\) * x^n * e^\(a*x\) - \(n / a\) * I_{n-1}. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Evaluation of int_0^1 x^4 * e^\(2x\) dx \(a = 2\):) Tj
T*
(   - Let J_n = int_0^1 x^n * e^\(2x\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - J_n = [ \(1/2\) * x^n * e^\(2x\) ]_0^1 - \(n / 2\) * J_{n-1}) Tj
T*
(   = [ \(1/2\) * 1^n * e^2 - 0 ] - \(n / 2\) * J_{n-1}) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/2\) * e^2 - \(n / 2\) * J_{n-1}.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute base case J_0:) Tj
T*
(   J_0 = int_0^1 e^\(2x\) dx = [ \(1/2\) * e^\(2x\) ]_0^1 = \(1/2\) * \(e^2 - 1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Compute J_1 \(n = 1\):) Tj
T*
(   J_1 = \(1/2\)*e^2 - \(1/2\)*J_0 = \(1/2\)*e^2 - \(1/4\)*\(e^2 - 1\) = \(1/4\)*e^2 + 1/4.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute J_2 \(n = 2\):) Tj
T*
(   J_2 = \(1/2\)*e^2 - \(2/2\)*J_1 = \(1/2\)*e^2 - J_1 = \(1/2\)*e^2 - \(1/4\)*e^2 - 1/4 = \(1/4\)*e^2 - 1/4.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute J_3 \(n = 3\):) Tj
T*
(   J_3 = \(1/2\)*e^2 - \(3/2\)*J_2 = \(1/2\)*e^2 - \(3/2\)*[ \(1/4\)*e^2 - 1/4 ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/2\)*e^2 - \(3/8\)*e^2 + 3/8 = \(1/8\)*e^2 + 3/8.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute J_4 \(n = 4\):) Tj
T*
(   J_4 = \(1/2\)*e^2 - \(4/2\)*J_3 = \(1/2\)*e^2 - 2 * [ \(1/8\)*e^2 + 3/8 ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/2\)*e^2 - \(1/4\)*e^2 - 3/4 = \(1/4\)*e^2 - 3/4) Tj
T*
(   = \(e^2 - 3\) / 4.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^1 x^4 * e^\(2x\) dx = \(e^2 - 3\) / 4 ~ \(7.389 - 3\) / 4 = 1.097.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
