(   - Integrate by parts: let u = x^n, dv = e^\(-x\) dx \(v = -e^\(-x\)\):) Tj
T*
(   du = n * x^\(n - 1\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Gamma\(n + 1\) = [ -x^n * e^\(-x\) ]_0^infinity - int_0^infinity \(-e^\(-x\)\) * [ n * x^\(n - 1\) ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = [ 0 - 0 ] + n * int_0^infinity e^\(-x\) * x^\(n - 1\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = n * Gamma\(n\). \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Deduction that Gamma\(n + 1\) = n!:) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluate Gamma\(1\):) Tj
T*
(   Gamma\(1\) = int_0^infinity e^\(-x\) * x^0 dx = int_0^infinity e^\(-x\) dx = [-e^\(-x\)]_0^infinity = 0) Tj
T*
(   - \(-1\) = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - By repeated application of recurrence:) Tj
T*
(   Gamma\(2\) = 1 * Gamma\(1\) = 1 = 1!) Tj
T*
(   Gamma\(3\) = 2 * Gamma\(2\) = 2 * 1! = 2!) Tj
T*
(   Gamma\(4\) = 3 * Gamma\(3\) = 3 * 2! = 3!) Tj
T*
(   In general, for any integer n >= 0:) Tj
T*
(   Gamma\(n + 1\) = n * \(n - 1\) * ... * 1 * Gamma\(1\) = n!.) Tj
T*
() Tj
