(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove Legendre's Duplication Formula for the Gamma function: Gamma\(m\) * Gamma\(m + 1/2\) = [ sqrt\(pi\) / 2^\(2m - 1\) ] * Gamma\(2m\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement:) Tj
T*
(   For any m > 0:) Tj
T*
(   Gamma\(m\) * Gamma\(m + 1/2\) = [ sqrt\(pi\) / 2^\(2m - 1\) ] * Gamma\(2m\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Proof:) Tj
T*
(   - Start with the trigonometric form of Beta\(m, m\):) Tj
T*
(   Beta\(m, m\) = 2 * int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^\(2m - 1\) theta * cos^\(2m - 1\) theta dtheta) Tj
T*
(   = 2 * int_0^\(pi/2\) [ sin theta * cos theta ]^\(2m - 1\) dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   - Use identity sin theta * cos theta = \(1/2\) * sin\(2*theta\):) Tj
T*
(   Beta\(m, m\) = 2 * int_0^\(pi/2\) [ \(1/2\) * sin\(2*theta\) ]^\(2m - 1\) dtheta) Tj
T*
(   = [ 2 / 2^\(2m - 1\) ] * int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^\(2m - 1\)\(2*theta\) dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute phi = 2*theta, dtheta = dphi / 2.) Tj
T*
(   When theta = 0, phi = 0; when theta = pi/2, phi = pi:) Tj
T*
(   Beta\(m, m\) = [ 1 / 2^\(2m - 1\) ] * int_0^pi sin^\(2m - 1\) phi dphi.) Tj
T*
(   - Since sin\(pi - phi\) = sin\(phi\), the integrand is symmetric about pi/2:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^pi sin^\(2m - 1\) phi dphi = 2 * int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^\(2m - 1\) phi dphi.) Tj
T*
(   - Express int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^\(2m - 1\) phi dphi in terms of Beta:) Tj
T*
(   2 * int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^\(2m - 1\) phi * cos^0 phi dphi = Beta\(m, 1/2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   Beta\(m, m\) = [ 1 / 2^\(2m - 1\) ] * Beta\(m, 1/2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Now express Beta functions in terms of Gamma functions:) Tj
T*
(   Beta\(m, m\) = [ Gamma\(m\) * Gamma\(m\) ] / Gamma\(2m\) = [Gamma\(m\)]^2 / Gamma\(2m\).) Tj
T*
(   Beta\(m, 1/2\) = [ Gamma\(m\) * Gamma\(1/2\) ] / Gamma\(m + 1/2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute Gamma\(1/2\) = sqrt\(pi\):) Tj
T*
(   Beta\(m, 1/2\) = [ Gamma\(m\) * sqrt\(pi\) ] / Gamma\(m + 1/2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Equate the two expressions:) Tj
T*
(   [Gamma\(m\)]^2 / Gamma\(2m\) = [ 1 / 2^\(2m - 1\) ] * [ Gamma\(m\) * sqrt\(pi\) ] / Gamma\(m + 1/2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Cancel one factor of Gamma\(m\) from both sides \(Gamma\(m\) != 0\):) Tj
T*
(   Gamma\(m\) / Gamma\(2m\) = sqrt\(pi\) / [ 2^\(2m - 1\) * Gamma\(m + 1/2\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Cross-multiply:) Tj
T*
(   Gamma\(m\) * Gamma\(m + 1/2\) = [ sqrt\(pi\) / 2^\(2m - 1\) ] * Gamma\(2m\).) Tj
T*
(   Hence proved.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
