(   For any non-integer p in \(0, 1\):) Tj
T*
(   Gamma\(p\) * Gamma\(1 - p\) = pi / sin\(p * pi\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Part \(i\): Evaluate Gamma\(1/4\) * Gamma\(3/4\):) Tj
T*
(   - Set p = 1/4 \(so 1 - p = 3/4\):) Tj
T*
(   Gamma\(1/4\) * Gamma\(3/4\) = pi / sin\(pi / 4\).) Tj
T*
(   - Since sin\(pi / 4\) = 1 / sqrt\(2\):) Tj
T*
(   Gamma\(1/4\) * Gamma\(3/4\) = pi / \(1 / sqrt\(2\)\) = pi * sqrt\(2\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Part \(ii\): Evaluate I = int_0^infinity [ 1 / \(1 + x^4\) ] dx:) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute x^4 = t => x = t^\(1/4\) => dx = \(1/4\) * t^\(-3/4\) dt.) Tj
T*
(   Limits: when x = 0, t = 0; when x -> infinity, t -> infinity.) Tj
T*
(   - I = int_0^infinity [ 1 / \(1 + t\) ] * \(1/4\) * t^\(-3/4\) dt) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/4\) * int_0^infinity [ t^\(1/4 - 1\) / \(1 + t\) ] dt.) Tj
T*
(   - Use the standard Beta function identity:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^infinity [ t^\(p - 1\) / \(1 + t\) ] dt = Beta\(p, 1 - p\) = Gamma\(p\) * Gamma\(1 - p\).) Tj
T*
(   - Here p = 1/4:) Tj
T*
(   I = \(1/4\) * Beta\(1/4, 3/4\) = \(1/4\) * [ Gamma\(1/4\) * Gamma\(3/4\) / Gamma\(1\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Using Gamma\(1\) = 1 and Gamma\(1/4\)*Gamma\(3/4\) = pi * sqrt\(2\):) Tj
T*
(   I = \(1/4\) * pi * sqrt\(2\) = pi / \(2 * sqrt\(2\)\).) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   \(i\) Gamma\(1/4\) * Gamma\(3/4\) = pi * sqrt\(2\).) Tj
T*
(   \(ii\) int_0^infinity [ 1 / \(1 + x^4\) ] dx = pi / \(2 * sqrt\(2\)\).) Tj
