(   [Problem Statement]: Evaluate the definite integrals using Beta and Gamma functions: \(i\) int_0^1 x^4 * \(1 - sqrt\(x\)\)^5 dx, and \(ii\) int_0^\(pi/2\) sqrt\(tan theta\) dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Part \(i\): Evaluate I1 = int_0^1 x^4 * \(1 - sqrt\(x\)\)^5 dx:) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute sqrt\(x\) = t => x = t^2 => dx = 2t dt.) Tj
T*
(   When x = 0, t = 0; when x = 1, t = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - x^4 = \(t^2\)^4 = t^8.) Tj
T*
(   - I1 = int_0^1 t^8 * \(1 - t\)^5 * \(2t dt\) = 2 * int_0^1 t^9 * \(1 - t\)^5 dt.) Tj
T*
(   - By definition of Beta function:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^1 t^\(10 - 1\) * \(1 - t\)^\(6 - 1\) dt = Beta\(10, 6\).) Tj
T*
(   - I1 = 2 * Beta\(10, 6\) = 2 * [ Gamma\(10\) * Gamma\(6\) ] / Gamma\(16\)) Tj
T*
(   = 2 * [ 9! * 5! ] / 15!) Tj
T*
(   = 2 * 5! / [ 15 * 14 * 13 * 12 * 11 * 10 ]) Tj
T*
(   = 2 * 120 / 3603600 = 240 / 3603600 = 1 / 15015.) Tj
T*
(   2. Part \(ii\): Evaluate I2 = int_0^\(pi/2\) sqrt\(tan theta\) dtheta:) Tj
T*
(   - Write tan theta = sin theta / cos theta:) Tj
T*
(   I2 = int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^\(1/2\) theta * cos^\(-1/2\) theta dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   - Using Wallis' Beta relation:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^\(pi/2\) sin^p theta * cos^q theta dtheta = \(1/2\) * Beta\(\(p + 1\)/2, \(q + 1\)/2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Here p = 1/2 => \(p + 1\)/2 = \(3/2\) / 2 = 3/4.) Tj
T*
(   Here q = -1/2 => \(q + 1\)/2 = \(1/2\) / 2 = 1/4.) Tj
T*
(   - I2 = \(1/2\) * Beta\(3/4, 1/4\) = \(1/2\) * [ Gamma\(3/4\) * Gamma\(1/4\) / Gamma\(1\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Using Euler's reflection formula: Gamma\(1/4\) * Gamma\(3/4\) = pi / sin\(pi/4\) = pi * sqrt\(2\):) Tj
T*
(   I2 = \(1/2\) * [ pi * sqrt\(2\) / 1 ] = pi / sqrt\(2\).) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   \(i\) int_0^1 x^4 * \(1 - sqrt\(x\)\)^5 dx = 1 / 15015.) Tj
T*
(   \(ii\) int_0^\(pi/2\) sqrt\(tan theta\) dtheta = pi / sqrt\(2\).) Tj
T*
