/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the Cartesian formula for arc length \(rectification\): s = int_a^b sqrt\(1 + \(dy/dx\)^2\) dx. Find the total perimeter of the astroid: x^\(2/3\) + y^\(2/3\) = a^\(2/3\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Cartesian Arc Length Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - Let y = f\(x\) be smooth on [a, b]. Partition [a, b] into n subintervals x0 < x1 < ... < xn) Tj
T*
(   with Delta_x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}.) Tj
T*
(   - The chord length between P_{i-1}\(x_{i-1}, y_{i-1}\) and P_i\(x_i, y_i\) is:) Tj
T*
(   Delta_s_i = sqrt\( \(Delta_x_i\)^2 + \(Delta_y_i\)^2 \) = sqrt\( 1 + \(Delta_y_i / Delta_x_i\)^2 \) *) Tj
T*
(   Delta_x_i.) Tj
T*
(   - By LMVT, Delta_y_i / Delta_x_i = f'\(c_i\) for some c_i in \(x_{i-1}, x_i\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total arc length s is the limit of Riemann sums as mesh size -> 0:) Tj
T*
(   s = lim_{n -> infinity} sum_{i=1}^n sqrt\( 1 + [f'\(c_i\)]^2 \) * Delta_x_i) Tj
T*
(   = int_a^b sqrt\( 1 + \(dy/dx\)^2 \) dx. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Rectification of the Astroid x^\(2/3\) + y^\(2/3\) = a^\(2/3\):) Tj
T*
(   - The astroid is symmetric in all four quadrants.) Tj
T*
(   Total Perimeter S = 4 * s_1 \(where s_1 is the arc length in the first quadrant x in [0, a]\).) Tj
T*
(   - Parametric equations:) Tj
T*
(   x = a * cos^3 t, y = a * sin^3 t, for t in [0, pi/2].) Tj
T*
(   - Derivatives:) Tj
T*
(   dx / dt = 3a * cos^2 t * \(-sin t\) = -3a * cos^2 t * sin t.) Tj
T*
(   dy / dt = 3a * sin^2 t * cos t.) Tj
T*
(   - Sum of squares:) Tj
T*
(   \(dx/dt\)^2 + \(dy/dt\)^2 = 9a^2 * cos^4 t * sin^2 t + 9a^2 * sin^4 t * cos^2 t) Tj
T*
(   = 9a^2 * sin^2 t * cos^2 t * \(cos^2 t + sin^2 t\)) Tj
T*
(   = 9a^2 * sin^2 t * cos^2 t.) Tj
T*
(   - Square root ds/dt:) Tj
T*
(   sqrt\(\(dx/dt\)^2 + \(dy/dt\)^2\) = 3a * sin t * cos t \(since sin t, cos t >= 0 on [0, pi/2]\).) Tj
T*
(   - Arc length in first quadrant:) Tj
T*
(   s_1 = int_0^\(pi/2\) 3a * sin t * cos t dt = 3a * [ \(sin^2 t\) / 2 ]_0^\(pi/2\) = 3a * \(1 / 2\) = 3a) Tj
T*
(   / 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Total Perimeter:) Tj
T*
(   S = 4 * s_1 = 4 * \(3a / 2\) = 6a.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The total perimeter of the astroid is 6a.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
