(   [Problem Statement]: Find the arc length of one complete arch of the cycloid: x = a * \(theta - sin theta\), y = a * \(1 - cos theta\) \(where theta ranges from 0 to 2*pi\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Compute parametric derivatives:) Tj
T*
(   x = a * \(theta - sin theta\) => dx / dtheta = a * \(1 - cos theta\).) Tj
T*
(   y = a * \(1 - cos theta\) => dy / dtheta = a * sin theta.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Form the differential arc length element ds:) Tj
T*
(   ds^2 = \(dx / dtheta\)^2 + \(dy / dtheta\)^2) Tj
T*
(   = a^2 * \(1 - cos theta\)^2 + a^2 * sin^2 theta) Tj
T*
(   = a^2 * [ 1 - 2*cos theta + cos^2 theta + sin^2 theta ]) Tj
T*
(   = a^2 * [ 2 - 2*cos theta ] = 2*a^2 * \(1 - cos theta\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Use half-angle identity 1 - cos theta = 2 * sin^2\(theta / 2\):) Tj
T*
ET

