12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the polar arc length formula: s = int_alpha^beta sqrt\(r^2 + \(dr/dtheta\)^2\) dtheta. Hence, compute the total perimeter of the cardioid r = a * \(1 + cos theta\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Polar Arc Length Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - x = r * cos theta, y = r * sin theta.) Tj
T*
(   - dx = \(r' cos theta - r sin theta\) dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   - dy = \(r' sin theta + r cos theta\) dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   - \(ds\)^2 = \(dx\)^2 + \(dy\)^2) Tj
T*
(   = [ \(r'\)^2 cos^2 theta - 2rr' cos theta sin theta + r^2 sin^2 theta ] dtheta^2) Tj
T*
(   + [ \(r'\)^2 sin^2 theta + 2rr' cos theta sin theta + r^2 cos^2 theta ] dtheta^2) Tj
T*
(   = [ \(r'\)^2 * \(cos^2 theta + sin^2 theta\) + r^2 * \(sin^2 theta + cos^2 theta\) ] dtheta^2) Tj
T*
(   = [ r^2 + \(r'\)^2 ] dtheta^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore: ds = sqrt\( r^2 + \(dr/dtheta\)^2 \) dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrating over [alpha, beta] yields: s = int_alpha^beta sqrt\(r^2 + \(dr/dtheta\)^2\) dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Total Perimeter of Cardioid r = a * \(1 + cos theta\):) Tj
T*
(   - By symmetry about the initial line, total perimeter S = 2 * int_0^pi ds.) Tj
T*
(   - r = a * \(1 + cos theta\) => dr / dtheta = -a * sin theta.) Tj
T*
(   - r^2 + \(r'\)^2 = a^2 * \(1 + cos theta\)^2 + a^2 * sin^2 theta) Tj
T*
(   = a^2 * [ 1 + 2*cos theta + cos^2 theta + sin^2 theta ]) Tj
T*
(   = a^2 * [ 2 + 2*cos theta ] = 2*a^2 * \(1 + cos theta\)) Tj
T*
(   = 4*a^2 * cos^2\(theta / 2\).) Tj
T*
(   - ds = sqrt\(4*a^2 * cos^2\(theta / 2\)\) = 2a * cos\(theta / 2\) dtheta \(since cos\(theta/2\) >= 0 on) Tj
T*
(   [0, pi]\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total Perimeter:) Tj
T*
(   S = 2 * int_0^pi 2a * cos\(theta / 2\) dtheta) Tj
T*
(   = 4a * [ 2 * sin\(theta / 2\) ]_0^pi) Tj
T*
(   = 8a * [ sin\(pi / 2\) - sin\(0\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = 8a * \(1 - 0\) = 8a.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The total perimeter of the cardioid is 8a.) Tj
T*
