ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Find the area bounded between the two intersecting parabolas y^2 = 4ax and x^2 = 4ay \(where a > 0\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Find points of intersection:) Tj
T*
(   From equation 1: y = x^2 / \(4a\).) Tj
T*
(   Substitute into equation 2: y^2 = 4ax => [ x^2 / \(4a\) ]^2 = 4ax) Tj
T*
(   => x^4 / \(16*a^2\) = 4ax) Tj
T*
(   => x^4 - 64*a^3 * x = 0) Tj
T*
(   => x * \(x^3 - 64*a^3\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Real roots: x = 0 and x = 4a.) Tj
T*
(   - At x = 0: y = 0. Point O\(0, 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - At x = 4a: y = \(4a\)^2 / \(4a\) = 4a. Point P\(4a, 4a\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Determine upper and lower bounding curves on [0, 4a]:) Tj
T*
(   - For y^2 = 4ax: y_upper = sqrt\(4ax\) = 2 * sqrt\(a\) * x^\(1/2\).) Tj
T*
(   - For x^2 = 4ay: y_lower = x^2 / \(4a\).) Tj
T*
(   - At test point x = a: y_upper = 2a, y_lower = a/4. Thus y_upper >= y_lower.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Set up the area integral:) Tj
T*
(   Area A = int_0^\(4a\) [ y_upper - y_lower ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = int_0^\(4a\) [ 2 * sqrt\(a\) * x^\(1/2\) - \(1 / \(4a\)\) * x^2 ] dx.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Integrate term-by-term:) Tj
T*
(   A = [ 2 * sqrt\(a\) * \(x^\(3/2\) / \(3/2\)\) - \(1 / \(4a\)\) * \(x^3 / 3\) ]_0^\(4a\)) Tj
T*
(   = [ \(4/3\) * sqrt\(a\) * x^\(3/2\) - \(1 / \(12a\)\) * x^3 ]_0^\(4a\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Substitute limits:) Tj
T*
(   - At x = 4a:) Tj
T*
(   x^\(3/2\) = \(4a\)^\(3/2\) = 8 * a^\(3/2\).) Tj
T*
(   First term = \(4/3\) * sqrt\(a\) * 8 * a^\(3/2\) = \(32/3\) * a^2.) Tj
T*
(   Second term = \(1 / \(12a\)\) * \(4a\)^3 = \(64 * a^3\) / \(12a\) = \(16/3\) * a^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Area:) Tj
T*
(   A = \(32/3\) * a^2 - \(16/3\) * a^2 = \(16/3\) * a^2.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The area enclosed between the two parabolas is 16*a^2 / 3.) Tj
T*
