(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Polar Area Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - In polar coordinates, consider an infinitesimal sector swept by radius vector r through an) Tj
T*
(   angle dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   - The sector approximates a circular sector of radius r and central angle dtheta:) Tj
T*
(   dA = \(1/2\) * r * \(r * dtheta\) = \(1/2\) * r^2 dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   - Total area from theta = alpha to theta = beta is obtained by summing these differential) Tj
T*
(   sectors:) Tj
T*
(   A = \(1/2\) * int_alpha^beta r^2 dtheta. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Computation for Cardioid r = a * \(1 + cos theta\):) Tj
T*
(   - By symmetry about the initial line theta = 0, the total area is:) Tj
T*
(   A = 2 * [ \(1/2\) * int_0^pi r^2 dtheta ] = int_0^pi r^2 dtheta.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute r = a * \(1 + cos theta\):) Tj
T*
(   r^2 = a^2 * \(1 + cos theta\)^2 = a^2 * \(1 + 2*cos theta + cos^2 theta\).) Tj
T*
(   - Use double-angle formula cos^2 theta = \(1 + cos 2theta\) / 2:) Tj
T*
(   r^2 = a^2 * [ 1 + 2*cos theta + 1/2 + \(1/2\)*cos 2theta ]) Tj
T*
(   = a^2 * [ 3/2 + 2*cos theta + \(1/2\)*cos 2theta ].) Tj
T*
(   - Integrate from 0 to pi:) Tj
T*
(   A = a^2 * int_0^pi [ 3/2 + 2*cos theta + \(1/2\)*cos 2theta ] dtheta) Tj
T*
(   = a^2 * [ \(3/2\)*theta + 2*sin theta + \(1/4\)*sin 2theta ]_0^pi.) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluate at limits:) Tj
T*
(   At pi: \(3/2\)*pi + 2*sin\(pi\) + \(1/4\)*sin\(2pi\) = \(3/2\)*pi + 0 + 0 = 3*pi / 2.) Tj
T*
(   At 0: 0.) Tj
T*
(   A = a^2 * \(3*pi / 2\) = \(3/2\) * pi * a^2.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The area enclosed by the cardioid is \(3/2\) * pi * a^2.) Tj
