(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the Cylindrical Shell Method for the volume of revolution about the y-axis: V = 2*pi * int_a^b x * y dx. Use this method to find the volume generated by revolving y = 4 - x^2 \(for 0 <= x <= 2\) about the y-axis.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Cylindrical Shell Method:) Tj
T*
(   - Let a region under y = f\(x\) from x = a to x = b \(0 <= a < b\) be revolved about the y-axis.) Tj
T*
(   - Consider a thin vertical strip at distance x with width dx and height y = f\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   - Revolving this strip about the y-axis produces a thin cylindrical shell:) Tj
T*
(   * Radius of shell = x.) Tj
T*
(   * Circumference = 2 * pi * x.) Tj
T*
(   * Height of shell = y = f\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   * Thickness of shell = dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Differential volume of shell:) Tj
T*
(   dV = Circumference * Height * Thickness = \(2 * pi * x\) * y * dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Total volume:) Tj
T*
(   V = 2 * pi * int_a^b x * y dx. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Computation for y = 4 - x^2 on [0, 2]:) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute y = 4 - x^2 into the formula:) Tj
T*
(   V = 2 * pi * int_0^2 x * \(4 - x^2\) dx) Tj
T*
(   = 2 * pi * int_0^2 \(4x - x^3\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluate the integral:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^2 \(4x - x^3\) dx = [ 2*x^2 - x^4 / 4 ]_0^2) Tj
T*
(   = [ 2*\(4\) - 16 / 4 ] - 0) Tj
T*
(   = 8 - 4 = 4.) Tj
T*
(   - Multiply by 2*pi:) Tj
T*
(   V = 2 * pi * 4 = 8 * pi.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The volume of the solid of revolution is 8*pi.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
