/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the formula for the surface area of a solid of revolution about the x-axis: S = 2*pi * int y * sqrt\(1 + \(y'\)^2\) dx. Use it to prove that the surface area of a sphere of radius R is 4 * pi * R^2.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Surface Area Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - When an arc element ds of curve y = f\(x\) is revolved about the x-axis, it generates the) Tj
T*
(   frustum of a thin cone.) Tj
T*
(   - The radius of revolution is y.) Tj
T*
(   - Differential surface area:) Tj
T*
(   dS = 2 * pi * \(radius\) * \(slant height\) = 2 * pi * y * ds.) Tj
T*
(   - In Cartesian coordinates, ds = sqrt\(1 + \(y'\)^2\) dx:) Tj
T*
(   dS = 2 * pi * y * sqrt\(1 + \(dy/dx\)^2\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Total surface area:) Tj
T*
(   S = 2 * pi * int_a^b y * sqrt\(1 + \(y'\)^2\) dx. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Proof for Surface Area of a Sphere:) Tj
T*
(   - Revolve the upper semicircle y = sqrt\(R^2 - x^2\) from x = -R to x = R about the x-axis.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute derivative:) Tj
T*
(   dy / dx = \(1/2\) * \(R^2 - x^2\)^\(-1/2\) * \(-2x\) = -x / sqrt\(R^2 - x^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Compute 1 + \(y'\)^2:) Tj
T*
(   1 + \(y'\)^2 = 1 + x^2 / \(R^2 - x^2\) = \(R^2 - x^2 + x^2\) / \(R^2 - x^2\) = R^2 / \(R^2 - x^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Form the integrand y * sqrt\(1 + \(y'\)^2\):) Tj
T*
(   y * sqrt\(1 + \(y'\)^2\) = sqrt\(R^2 - x^2\) * [ R / sqrt\(R^2 - x^2\) ] = R \(constant!\).) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
