(   [Problem Statement]: State Leibniz's Rule for differentiation under the integral sign with variable limits. Use it to evaluate the Frullani integral: int_0^infinity [ \(e^\(-a*x\) - e^\(-b*x\)\) / x ] dx \(where a, b > 0\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Leibniz's Rule for Differentiation of an Integral:) Tj
T*
(   - Let I\(alpha\) = int_{u\(alpha\)}^{v\(alpha\)} f\(x, alpha\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - If f and df/dalpha are continuous, then:) Tj
T*
(   d/dalpha [ I\(alpha\) ] = f\(v\(alpha\), alpha\) * v'\(alpha\) - f\(u\(alpha\), alpha\) * u'\(alpha\) +) Tj
T*
(   int_{u\(alpha\)}^{v\(alpha\)} [ df / dalpha ] dx.) Tj
T*
(   2. Evaluation of Frullani Integral using Differentiation:) Tj
T*
(   - Let I\(a\) = int_0^infinity [ \(e^\(-a*x\) - e^\(-b*x\)\) / x ] dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Note that when a = b, I\(b\) = int_0^infinity 0 dx = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Differentiate I\(a\) with respect to parameter a:) Tj
T*
(   dI / da = int_0^infinity d/da [ \(e^\(-a*x\) - e^\(-b*x\)\) / x ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = int_0^infinity [ \(-x * e^\(-a*x\)\) / x ] dx) Tj
T*
(   = - int_0^infinity e^\(-a*x\) dx.) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluate this elementary integral:) Tj
T*
(   - int_0^infinity e^\(-a*x\) dx = - [ - \(1/a\) * e^\(-a*x\) ]_0^infinity = \(1/a\) * [ 0 - 1 ] = -1/a.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   dI / da = -1 / a.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrate with respect to a:) Tj
T*
(   I\(a\) = - ln\(a\) + C.) Tj
T*
(   - Apply boundary condition I\(b\) = 0:) Tj
T*
(   0 = - ln\(b\) + C => C = ln\(b\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute C:) Tj
T*
(   I\(a\) = - ln\(a\) + ln\(b\) = ln\(b / a\).) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   int_0^infinity [ \(e^\(-a*x\) - e^\(-b*x\)\) / x ] dx = ln\(b / a\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
