12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive Simpson's 1/3 Rule for numerical integration from the Lagrange quadratic interpolating polynomial. Analyze its order of accuracy and error term.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Simpson's 1/3 Rule:) Tj
T*
(   - Let [a, b] be divided into an even number n of equal subintervals of width h = \(b - a\) / n.) Tj
T*
(   - Consider a single double-interval [x0, x2] with three points x0, x1 = x0 + h, x2 = x0 + 2h.) Tj
T*
(   - Approximate f\(x\) by a quadratic polynomial P2\(x\) passing through \(x0, y0\), \(x1, y1\), \(x2,) Tj
T*
(   y2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Shift coordinates for simplicity: set t = 0 at x1, so x0 corresponds to t = -h, x1 to t = 0,) Tj
T*
(   x2 to t = h.) Tj
T*
(   Let P2\(t\) = A*t^2 + B*t + C.) Tj
T*
(   - At t = -h: y0 = A*h^2 - B*h + C.) Tj
T*
(   - At t = 0: y1 = C.) Tj
T*
(   - At t = h: y2 = A*h^2 + B*h + C.) Tj
T*
(   - Add y0 and y2:) Tj
T*
(   y0 + y2 = 2*A*h^2 + 2*C = 2*A*h^2 + 2*y1 => 2*A*h^2 = y0 + y2 - 2*y1.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
