(   - Integrate P2\(t\) from -h to h:) Tj
T*
(   int_{-h}^h \(A*t^2 + B*t + C\) dt = [ A*t^3 / 3 + B*t^2 / 2 + C*t ]_{-h}^h) Tj
T*
(   = \(2/3\)*A*h^3 + 2*C*h = \(h / 3\) * [ 2*A*h^2 + 6*C ].) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute 2*A*h^2 = y0 + y2 - 2*y1 and C = y1:) Tj
T*
(   int_{x0}^{x2} f\(x\) dx ~ \(h / 3\) * [ \(y0 + y2 - 2*y1\) + 6*y1 ] = \(h / 3\) * [ y0 + 4*y1 + y2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Summing over all n/2 double-subintervals gives the Composite Simpson's 1/3 Rule:) Tj
T*
(   int_a^b f\(x\) dx ~ \(h / 3\) * [ \(y0 + yn\) + 4*\(y1 + y3 + ... + y_{n-1}\) + 2*\(y2 + y4 + ... +) Tj
T*
(   y_{n-2}\) ].) Tj
T*
(   2. Error Term and Degree of Precision:) Tj
T*
(   - By Taylor series expansion, the cubic term cancels due to symmetry!) Tj
T*
(   - Local error for one pair of intervals: E_local = - \(h^5 / 90\) * f^\(4\)\(xi\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total global error:) Tj
T*
(   E_global = - [ \(b - a\) * h^4 / 180 ] * f^\(4\)\(eta\) = O\(h^4\).) Tj
T*
(   - Simpson's 1/3 rule has degree of precision 3: it integrates polynomials up to degree 3) Tj
T*
(   \(cubic\) exactly.) Tj
