/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: In biotechnology and pharmacokinetics, define Area Under the Curve \(AUC\). Calculate total AUC\(0 to infinity\) and clearance Cl for a two-compartment intravenous drug bolus C\(t\) = 50*e^\(-1.5*t\) + 20*e^\(-0.2*t\) \(mg/L, t in hours\) with an initial dose D = 500 mg.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Pharmacokinetic Foundations:) Tj
T*
(   - Area Under the Curve \(AUC\) represents total systemic drug exposure over time:) Tj
T*
(   AUC_{0 -> infinity} = int_0^infinity C\(t\) dt.) Tj
T*
(   - Clearance \(Cl\) is the volume of plasma completely cleared of drug per unit time:) Tj
T*
(   Cl = Dose / AUC_{0 -> infinity}.) Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step AUC Evaluation:) Tj
T*
(   - Given: C\(t\) = 50 * e^\(-1.5*t\) + 20 * e^\(-0.2*t\).) Tj
T*
(   - AUC_{0 -> infinity} = int_0^infinity [ 50 * e^\(-1.5*t\) + 20 * e^\(-0.2*t\) ] dt) Tj
T*
(   = 50 * int_0^infinity e^\(-1.5*t\) dt + 20 * int_0^infinity e^\(-0.2*t\) dt.) Tj
T*
(   - For any exponential decay int_0^infinity e^\(-k*t\) dt = 1 / k:) Tj
T*
(   First integral = 50 / 1.5 = 50 / \(3/2\) = 100 / 3 = 33.333 mg*h / L.) Tj
T*
(   Second integral = 20 / 0.2 = 20 / \(1/5\) = 100.000 mg*h / L.) Tj
T*
(   - Total AUC:) Tj
T*
(   AUC_{0 -> infinity} = 33.333 + 100.000 = 133.333 mg*h / L \(or 400 / 3 mg*h / L\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Total Clearance \(Cl\) Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   - Dose D = 500 mg.) Tj
T*
(   - Cl = Dose / AUC = 500 mg / \(400 / 3 mg*h / L\)) Tj
T*
(   = 500 * \(3 / 400\) L / h = 1500 / 400 L / h = 3.75 L / h.) Tj
T*
(   4. Mean Residence Time \(MRT\):) Tj
T*
(   - AUMC = int_0^infinity t * C\(t\) dt.) Tj
T*
(   int_0^infinity t * e^\(-k*t\) dt = Gamma\(2\) / k^2 = 1 / k^2.) Tj
T*
(   AUMC = 50 / \(1.5\)^2 + 20 / \(0.2\)^2 = 50 / 2.25 + 20 / 0.04 = 22.22 + 500 = 522.22 mg*h^2 / L.) Tj
T*
(   - MRT = AUMC / AUC = 522.22 / 133.33 = 3.92 hours.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
